      "difficulty_level": "H3",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author realizes Dunkl matching coefficients through the dual of the matching-product map, identifies the complete-graph polynomial span with the two-row Specht module in each degree, and matches the resulting Catalan-triangle Hilbert series to a linear/quadratic square-zero algebra presentation. These duality/representation/presentation forms are one foundation object. Later arbitrary-graph saturation and unicyclic applications are context, not additional counts.",
